        "Now the same-day half nobody is connecting to it.  Business Insider reviewed dozens of sponsored posts and spoke to six managers and creators.  <mark>Sponsored Instagram posts promoting ChatGPT went from 61 in June to 122 in July to 141 in August, according to the creator analytics company HypeAuditor.</mark>  The targets are parenting and fitness creators alongside technology ones.  The pitch, in the words of a talent manager and of one campaign brief seen by Business Insider, is to show why ChatGPT is cool, or how it supports work that is good for the world.  The Shade Room, a meme account with more than 28 million Instagram followers, ran a ChatGPT-made word search in early September.",
